type: bullet-list
title: Engineering Principles

- Design for testability first: Write code that is easy to verify in isolation, not just in the happy path
  - Isolate side effects
  - Prefer pure functions
- Minimal scope per change: One concern per commit, one reason to revert
- Read before editing
  - Skim the call sites
  - Check for side effects
- Verify your work: Run the linter, the tests, and review the diff before declaring done
- Update docs alongside code
